Mutable Instruments' Braids (braids/) and stmlib (stmlib/), as used by TONIC's BRAIDS engine.
Sources: https://github.com/pichenettes/eurorack (braids, commit f4cfa76) and https://github.com/pichenettes/stmlib
(commit d18def8). TONIC's changes: the digital oscillator's delay lines outside it (shared by voices), the comb
delay 4096 samples long (for 44.1 kHz); signature_waveshaper.h unchanged (0.15); stmlib's Random keeps a state
per CPU core (0.16); digital_oscillator.cc's absolute frequencies (VOSIM, VOWEL, VFOF, the noise models' period)
raised for 44.1 kHz (0.17); braids_voice.{h,cc} and shim/ are TONIC's own (MPL-2.0).

